 "name": "Volumetric Lighting Lab e01: light shafts",
 "_note": "Light shafts. An enclosed hall -- walls, and a roof of planks with slits between them -- under a high sun: the only lit air inside is the air the slits let the sun into, so the shafts are the shadow map seen in the medium, which a fog overlay cannot draw. (The first fixture, an open colonnade, lit nearly all of its air and read as a white-out: shafts need the light blocked for most of the volume.) A spot behind a grille at the far end throws barred beams down the hall.",
